@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About · MHGU LookUp</PageTitle>

<div class="page roomy about">
    <div style="max-width: 720px">
        <h1 class="page-title" style="margin: 0 0 12px">MHGU LookUp</h1>
        <p>
            A reference app for <strong>Monster Hunter Generations Ultimate</strong>: monsters, quests, weapons, armor, decorations, armor skills,
            Hunting Styles, Hunter Arts and items, with more tabs filled in as their data is read from the game.
            Created by <strong>Armored_Raven</strong>, as the GU sibling of the MHFU LookUp.
        </p>

        <h2>This version</h2>
        <p>
            This is the C# version of the app, built with Blazor WebAssembly: it runs on .NET in the browser, as a static site with no server.
            It reads the same data files as the <a href="@Nav.ReactAppUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener">original React version</a>.
            The source is on <a href="https://github.com/ArmoredRaven17/mhgu-lookup-blazor" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
        <p>
            Every name, description and value is read from the game's own text and data tables (dumped from a
            personally-owned copy). Nothing is carried over from the MHFU app or taken from guides; community
            databases were used only to check that a table had been read right. No game files are redistributed.
        </p>
        <p>
            Two things on the Monsters tab are not the game's: the hit-zone names, which come from the community
            (the game has no names for them), and which class each monster belongs to (the class names are the
            game's, the assignment was made by hand). The monster data itself was read from the game by the MHGU
            Monster Viewer.
        </p>
        <p>
            The short armor and food skill explanations are written from the ones in MHGU Armor Skills Explained,
            which were read from the game's code and data the same way; each skill links to its full explanation there.
        </p>

        <h2>Development</h2>
        <p>
            Built with substantial help from <a href="https://claude.com/claude-code" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Claude Code</a>,
            Anthropic's AI coding tool: most of the code, the data tools and the text were written with AI assistance,
            directed and reviewed by the author. Errors may remain; verify any value you rely on.
        </p>

        <h2>Credits</h2>
        <p>
            The app shell (layout, search, bookmarks, notes, settings) comes from the MHFU LookUp. The MHFU display
            font is a fan-made recreation of the Monster Hunter interface typeface; the menu textures are carried
            over from the sibling apps.
        </p>

